Results
The results of a series of computations performed to validate the algorithmand to illustratethe potentialof RAGD are now presented. In all cases a cubic computational domain, tessellated into equalsized cubic cells, was used to capture the vorticity in the rotor wake. Potential improvements in the performance of the code that might result from local grid re nement or distortion of the cells to match better the inherent geometry of the rotors and wake will not be investigated in this paper. Throughout, zero-curvature conditions were simultaneously imposed on the vorticity and velocity on all boundaries of the computational domain. The ill-posed nature of Eq. (2) with these boundary conditions is resolved by collocation
